23.5:
You prepare a table before me in the presence of my enemies;
You anoint my head with oil;
My cup runs over.

25.2:
O my God, I trust in You;
Let me not be ashamed;
Let not my enemies triumph over me.

25.5:
Lead me in Your truth and teach me,
For You are the God of my salvation;
On You I wait all the day.

25.7:
Do not remember the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions;
According to Your mercy remember me,
For Your goodness’ sake, O Lord.

27.1:
The Lord is my light and my salvation;
Whom shall I fear?
The Lord is the strength of my life;
Of whom shall I be afraid?

27.5:
For in the time of trouble
He shall hide me in His pavilion;
In the secret place of His tabernacle
He shall hide me;
He shall set me high upon a rock.

27.6:
And now my head shall be lifted up above my enemies all around me;
Therefore I will offer sacrifices of joy in His tabernacle;
I will sing, yes, I will sing praises to the Lord.

27.9:
Do not hide Your face from me;
Do not turn Your servant away in anger;
You have been my help;
Do not leave me nor forsake me,
O God of my salvation.

27.12:
Do not deliver me to the will of my adversaries;
For false witnesses have risen against me,
And such as breathe out violence.

27.14:
Wait on the Lord;
Be of good courage,
And He shall strengthen your heart;
Wait, I say, on the Lord!

28.4:
Give them according to their deeds,
And according to the wickedness of their endeavors;
Give them according to the work of their hands;
Render to them what they deserve.

28.7:
The Lord is my strength and my shield;
My heart trusted in Him, and I am helped;
Therefore my heart greatly rejoices,
And with my song I will praise Him.

29.3:
The voice of the Lord is over the waters;
The God of glory thunders;
The Lord is over many waters.

29.9:
The voice of the Lord makes the deer give birth,
And strips the forests bare;
And in His temple everyone says, “Glory!”

31.1:
In You, O Lord, I put my trust;
Let me never be ashamed;
Deliver me in Your righteousness.

31.3:
For You are my rock and my fortress;
Therefore, for Your name’s sake,
Lead me and guide me.

31.7:
I will be glad and rejoice in Your mercy,
For You have considered my trouble;
You have known my soul in adversities,

31.9:
Have mercy on me, O Lord, for I am in trouble;
My eye wastes away with grief,
Yes, my soul and my body!

31.13:
For I hear the slander of many;
Fear is on every side;
While they take counsel together against me,
They scheme to take away my life.

31.15:
My times are in Your hand;
Deliver me from the hand of my enemies,
And from those who persecute me.

31.17:
Do not let me be ashamed, O Lord, for I have called upon You;
Let the wicked be ashamed;
Let them be silent in the grave.

32.7:
You are my hiding place;
You shall preserve me from trouble;
You shall surround me with songs of deliverance. Selah

35.8:
Let destruction come upon him unexpectedly,
And let his net that he has hidden catch himself;
Into that very destruction let him fall.

35.13:
But as for me, when they were sick,
My clothing was sackcloth;
I humbled myself with fasting;
And my prayer would return to my own heart.

35.15:
But in my adversity they rejoiced
And gathered together;
Attackers gathered against me,
And I did not know it;
They tore at me and did not cease;

35.22:
This You have seen, O Lord;
Do not keep silence.
O Lord, do not be far from me.

36.4:
He devises wickedness on his bed;
He sets himself in a way that is not good;
He does not abhor evil.

36.6:
Your righteousness is like the great mountains;
Your judgments are a great deep;
O Lord, You preserve man and beast.

37.7:
Rest in the Lord, and wait patiently for Him;
Do not fret because of him who prospers in his way,
Because of the man who brings wicked schemes to pass.

37.9:
For evildoers shall be cut off;
But those who wait on the Lord,
They shall inherit the earth.

37.10:
For yet a little while and the wicked shall be no more;
Indeed, you will look carefully for his place,
But it shall be no more.

37.25:
I have been young, and now am old;
Yet I have not seen the righteous forsaken,
Nor his descendants begging bread.

38.12:
Those also who seek my life lay snares for me;
Those who seek my hurt speak of destruction,
And plan deception all the day long.

39.2:
I was mute with silence,
I held my peace even from good;
And my sorrow was stirred up.

39.3:
My heart was hot within me;
While I was musing, the fire burned.
Then I spoke with my tongue:

39.5:
Indeed, You have made my days as handbreadths,
And my age is as nothing before You;
Certainly every man at his best state is but vapor. Selah

39.6:
Surely every man walks about like a shadow;
Surely they busy themselves in vain;
He heaps up riches,
And does not know who will gather them.

39.11:
When with rebukes You correct man for iniquity,
You make his beauty melt away like a moth;
Surely every man is vapor. Selah

39.12:
“Hear my prayer, O Lord,
And give ear to my cry;
Do not be silent at my tears;
For I am a stranger with You,
A sojourner, as all my fathers were.

40.1:
I waited patiently for the Lord;
And He inclined to me,
And heard my cry.

40.5:
Many, O Lord my God, are Your wonderful works
Which You have done;
And Your thoughts toward us
Cannot be recounted to You in order;
If I would declare and speak of them,
They are more than can be numbered.

40.6:
Sacrifice and offering You did not desire;
My ears You have opened.
Burnt offering and sin offering You did not require.

40.10:
I have not hidden Your righteousness within my heart;
I have declared Your faithfulness and Your salvation;
I have not concealed Your lovingkindness and Your truth
From the great assembly.

40.12:
For innumerable evils have surrounded me;
My iniquities have overtaken me, so that I am not able to look up;
They are more than the hairs of my head;
Therefore my heart fails me.

40.16:
Let all those who seek You rejoice and be glad in You;
Let such as love Your salvation say continually,
“The Lord be magnified!”

40.17:
But I am poor and needy;
Yet the Lord thinks upon me.
You are my help and my deliverer;
Do not delay, O my God.

41.2:
The Lord will preserve him and keep him alive,
And he will be blessed on the earth;
You will not deliver him to the will of his enemies.

41.6:
And if he comes to see me, he speaks lies;
His heart gathers iniquity to itself;
When he goes out, he tells it.

43.1:
Vindicate me, O God,
And plead my cause against an ungodly nation;
Oh, deliver me from the deceitful and unjust man!

43.2:
For You are the God of my strength;
Why do You cast me off?
Why do I go mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?

44.2:
You drove out the nations with Your hand,
But them You planted;
You afflicted the peoples, and cast them out.

44.17:
All this has come upon us;
But we have not forgotten You,
Nor have we dealt falsely with Your covenant.

45.1:
My heart is overflowing with a good theme;
I recite my composition concerning the King;
My tongue is the pen of a ready writer.

45.2:
You are fairer than the sons of men;
Grace is poured upon Your lips;
Therefore God has blessed You forever.

45.7:
You love righteousness and hate wickedness;
Therefore God, Your God, has anointed You
With the oil of gladness more than Your companions.

45.10:
Listen, O daughter,
Consider and incline your ear;
Forget your own people also, and your father’s house;

46.2:
Therefore we will not fear,
Even though the earth be removed,
And though the mountains be carried into the midst of the sea;

46.9:
He makes wars cease to the end of the earth;
He breaks the bow and cuts the spear in two;
He burns the chariot in the fire.

46.10:
Be still, and know that I am God;
I will be exalted among the nations,
I will be exalted in the earth!

48.10:
According to Your name, O God,
So is Your praise to the ends of the earth;
Your right hand is full of righteousness.

48.12:
Walk about Zion,
And go all around her.
Count her towers;

48.13:
Mark well her bulwarks;
Consider her palaces;
That you may tell it to the generation following.

49.10:
For he sees wise men die;
Likewise the fool and the senseless person perish,
And leave their wealth to others.

49.11:
Their inner thought is that their houses will last forever,
Their dwelling places to all generations;
They call their lands after their own names.

49.14:
Like sheep they are laid in the grave;
Death shall feed on them;
The upright shall have dominion over them in the morning;
And their beauty shall be consumed in the grave, far from their dwelling.

50.3:
Our God shall come, and shall not keep silent;
A fire shall devour before Him,
And it shall be very tempestuous all around Him.

50.7:
“Hear, O My people, and I will speak,
O Israel, and I will testify against you;
I am God, your God!

50.21:
These things you have done, and I kept silent;
You thought that I was altogether like you;
But I will rebuke you,
And set them in order before your eyes.

50.23:
Whoever offers praise glorifies Me;
And to him who orders his conduct aright
I will show the salvation of God.”

51.19:
Then You shall be pleased with the sacrifices of righteousness,
With burnt offering and whole burnt offering;
Then they shall offer bulls on Your altar.

52.5:
God shall likewise destroy you forever;
He shall take you away, and pluck you out of your dwelling place,
And uproot you from the land of the living. Selah

53.3:
Every one of them has turned aside;
They have together become corrupt;
There is none who does good,
No, not one.

54.3:
For strangers have risen up against me,
And oppressors have sought after my life;
They have not set God before them. Selah

55.12:
For it is not an enemy who reproaches me;
Then I could bear it.
Nor is it one who hates me who has exalted himself against me;
Then I could hide from him.

55.15:
Let death seize them;
Let them go down alive into hell,
For wickedness is in their dwellings and among them.

55.22:
Cast your burden on the Lord,
And He shall sustain you;
He shall never permit the righteous to be moved.

55.23:
But You, O God, shall bring them down to the pit of destruction;
Bloodthirsty and deceitful men shall not live out half their days;
But I will trust in You.

56.8:
You number my wanderings;
Put my tears into Your bottle;
Are they not in Your book?

56.9:
When I cry out to You,
Then my enemies will turn back;
This I know, because God is for me.

56.11:
In God I have put my trust;
I will not be afraid.
What can man do to me?

57.3:
He shall send from heaven and save me;
He reproaches the one who would swallow me up. Selah
God shall send forth His mercy and His truth.

57.6:
They have prepared a net for my steps;
My soul is bowed down;
They have dug a pit before me;
Into the midst of it they themselves have fallen. Selah

58.7:
Let them flow away as waters which run continually;
When he bends his bow,
Let his arrows be as if cut in pieces.

58.11:
So that men will say,
“Surely there is a reward for the righteous;
Surely He is God who judges in the earth.”

59.3:
For look, they lie in wait for my life;
The mighty gather against me,
Not for my transgression nor for my sin, O Lord.

59.5:
You therefore, O Lord God of hosts, the God of Israel,
Awake to punish all the nations;
Do not be merciful to any wicked transgressors. Selah

59.7:
Indeed, they belch with their mouth;
Swords are in their lips;
For they say, “Who hears?”

59.16:
But I will sing of Your power;
Yes, I will sing aloud of Your mercy in the morning;
For You have been my defense
And refuge in the day of my trouble.

59.17:
To You, O my Strength, I will sing praises;
For God is my defense,
My God of mercy.

60.1:
O God, You have cast us off;
You have broken us down;
You have been displeased;
Oh, restore us again!

60.2:
You have made the earth tremble;
You have broken it;
Heal its breaches, for it is shaking.

60.7:
Gilead is Mine, and Manasseh is Mine;
Ephraim also is the helmet for My head;
Judah is My lawgiver.

60.8:
Moab is My washpot;
Over Edom I will cast My shoe;
Philistia, shout in triumph because of Me.”

61.2:
From the end of the earth I will cry to You,
When my heart is overwhelmed;
Lead me to the rock that is higher than I.

62.2:
He only is my rock and my salvation;
He is my defense;
I shall not be greatly moved.

62.4:
They only consult to cast him down from his high position;
They delight in lies;
They bless with their mouth,
But they curse inwardly. Selah

62.6:
He only is my rock and my salvation;
He is my defense;
I shall not be moved.

62.7:
In God is my salvation and my glory;
The rock of my strength,
And my refuge, is in God.

62.8:
Trust in Him at all times, you people;
Pour out your heart before Him;
God is a refuge for us. Selah

63.1:
O God, You are my God;
Early will I seek You;
My soul thirsts for You;
My flesh longs for You
In a dry and thirsty land
Where there is no water.

63.11:
But the king shall rejoice in God;
Everyone who swears by Him shall glory;
But the mouth of those who speak lies shall be stopped.

64.5:
They encourage themselves in an evil matter;
They talk of laying snares secretly;
They say, “Who will see them?”

64.9:
All men shall fear,
And shall declare the work of God;
For they shall wisely consider His doing.

65.3:
Iniquities prevail against me;
As for our transgressions,
You will provide atonement for them.

65.9:
You visit the earth and water it,
You greatly enrich it;
The river of God is full of water;
You provide their grain,
For so You have prepared it.

65.13:
The pastures are clothed with flocks;
The valleys also are covered with grain;
They shout for joy, they also sing.

66.4:
All the earth shall worship You
And sing praises to You;
They shall sing praises to Your name.” Selah

66.6:
He turned the sea into dry land;
They went through the river on foot.
There we will rejoice in Him.

66.7:
He rules by His power forever;
His eyes observe the nations;
Do not let the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah

66.12:
You have caused men to ride over our heads;
We went through fire and through water;
But You brought us out to rich fulfillment.

66.15:
I will offer You burnt sacrifices of fat animals,
With the sweet aroma of rams;
I will offer bulls with goats. Selah

68.1:
Let God arise,
Let His enemies be scattered;
Let those also who hate Him flee before Him.

68.3:
But let the righteous be glad;
Let them rejoice before God;
Yes, let them rejoice exceedingly.

68.6:
God sets the solitary in families;
He brings out those who are bound into prosperity;
But the rebellious dwell in a dry land.

68.8:
The earth shook;
The heavens also dropped rain at the presence of God;
Sinai itself was moved at the presence of God, the God of Israel.

68.16:
Why do you fume with envy, you mountains of many peaks?
This is the mountain which God desires to dwell in;
Yes, the Lord will dwell in it forever.

68.17:
The chariots of God are twenty thousand,
Even thousands of thousands;
The Lord is among them as in Sinai, in the Holy Place.

68.34:
Ascribe strength to God;
His excellence is over Israel,
And His strength is in the clouds.

69.3:
I am weary with my crying;
My throat is dry;
My eyes fail while I wait for my God.

69.4:
Those who hate me without a cause
Are more than the hairs of my head;
They are mighty who would destroy me,
Being my enemies wrongfully;
Though I have stolen nothing,
I still must restore it.

69.15:
Let not the floodwater overflow me,
Nor let the deep swallow me up;
And let not the pit shut its mouth on me.

69.17:
And do not hide Your face from Your servant,
For I am in trouble;
Hear me speedily.

69.20:
Reproach has broken my heart,
And I am full of heaviness;
I looked for someone to take pity, but there was none;
And for comforters, but I found none.

70.4:
Let all those who seek You rejoice and be glad in You;
And let those who love Your salvation say continually,
“Let God be magnified!”

70.5:
But I am poor and needy;
Make haste to me, O God!
You are my help and my deliverer;
O Lord, do not delay.

71.6:
By You I have been upheld from birth;
You are He who took me out of my mother’s womb.
My praise shall be continually of You.

71.19:
Also Your righteousness, O God, is very high,
You who have done great things;
O God, who is like You?

72.4:
He will bring justice to the poor of the people;
He will save the children of the needy,
And will break in pieces the oppressor.

72.15:
And He shall live;
And the gold of Sheba will be given to Him;
Prayer also will be made for Him continually,
And daily He shall be praised.

72.16:
There will be an abundance of grain in the earth,
On the top of the mountains;
Its fruit shall wave like Lebanon;
And those of the city shall flourish like grass of the earth.

72.17:
His name shall endure forever;
His name shall continue as long as the sun.
And men shall be blessed in Him;
All nations shall call Him blessed.

73.12:
Behold, these are the ungodly,
Who are always at ease;
They increase in riches.

73.28:
But it is good for me to draw near to God;
I have put my trust in the Lord God,
That I may declare all Your works.

74.9:
We do not see our signs;
There is no longer any prophet;
Nor is there any among us who knows how long.

75.8:
For in the hand of the Lord there is a cup,
And the wine is red;
It is fully mixed, and He pours it out;
Surely its dregs shall all the wicked of the earth
Drain and drink down.

76.5:
The stouthearted were plundered;
They have sunk into their sleep;
And none of the mighty men have found the use of their hands.

76.7:
You, Yourself, are to be feared;
And who may stand in Your presence
When once You are angry?

77.1:
I cried out to God with my voice—
To God with my voice;
And He gave ear to me.

77.2:
In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord;
My hand was stretched out in the night without ceasing;
My soul refused to be comforted.

77.6:
I call to remembrance my song in the night;
I meditate within my heart,
And my spirit makes diligent search.

77.16:
The waters saw You, O God;
The waters saw You, they were afraid;
The depths also trembled.

77.17:
The clouds poured out water;
The skies sent out a sound;
Your arrows also flashed about.

77.18:
The voice of Your thunder was in the whirlwind;
The lightnings lit up the world;
The earth trembled and shook.

78.7:
That they may set their hope in God,
And not forget the works of God,
But keep His commandments;

78.21:
Therefore the Lord heard this and was furious;
So a fire was kindled against Jacob,
And anger also came up against Israel,

78.50:
He made a path for His anger;
He did not spare their soul from death,
But gave their life over to the plague,

79.1:
O God, the nations have come into Your inheritance;
Your holy temple they have defiled;
They have laid Jerusalem in heaps.

79.11:
Let the groaning of the prisoner come before You;
According to the greatness of Your power
Preserve those who are appointed to die;

79.13:
So we, Your people and sheep of Your pasture,
Will give You thanks forever;
We will show forth Your praise to all generations.

80.1:
Give ear, O Shepherd of Israel,
You who lead Joseph like a flock;
You who dwell between the cherubim, shine forth!

80.3:
Restore us, O God;
Cause Your face to shine,
And we shall be saved!

80.7:
Restore us, O God of hosts;
Cause Your face to shine,
And we shall be saved!

80.14:
Return, we beseech You, O God of hosts;
Look down from heaven and see,
And visit this vine

80.19:
Restore us, O Lord God of hosts;
Cause Your face to shine,
And we shall be saved!

81.7:
You called in trouble, and I delivered you;
I answered you in the secret place of thunder;
I tested you at the waters of Meribah. Selah

81.10:
I am the Lord your God,
Who brought you out of the land of Egypt;
Open your mouth wide, and I will fill it.

82.5:
They do not know, nor do they understand;
They walk about in darkness;
All the foundations of the earth are unstable.

84.2:
My soul longs, yes, even faints
For the courts of the Lord;
My heart and my flesh cry out for the living God.

84.6:
As they pass through the Valley of Baca,
They make it a spring;
The rain also covers it with pools.

84.11:
For the Lord God is a sun and shield;
The Lord will give grace and glory;
No good thing will He withhold
From those who walk uprightly.

86.2:
Preserve my life, for I am holy;
You are my God;
Save Your servant who trusts in You!

86.11:
Teach me Your way, O Lord;
I will walk in Your truth;
Unite my heart to fear Your name.

87.4:
“I will make mention of Rahab and Babylon to those who know Me;
Behold, O Philistia and Tyre, with Ethiopia:
‘This one was born there.’ ”

87.5:
And of Zion it will be said,
“This one and that one were born in her;
And the Most High Himself shall establish her.”

88.8:
You have put away my acquaintances far from me;
You have made me an abomination to them;
I am shut up, and I cannot get out;

88.9:
My eye wastes away because of affliction. 
Lord, I have called daily upon You;
I have stretched out my hands to You.

88.15:
I have been afflicted and ready to die from my youth;
I suffer Your terrors;
I am distraught.

89.19:
Then You spoke in a vision to Your holy one,
And said: “I have given help to one who is mighty;
I have exalted one chosen from the people.

90.5:
You carry them away like a flood;
They are like a sleep.
In the morning they are like grass which grows up:

90.10:
The days of our lives are seventy years;
And if by reason of strength they are eighty years,
Yet their boast is only labor and sorrow;
For it is soon cut off, and we fly away.

90.17:
And let the beauty of the Lord our God be upon us,
And establish the work of our hands for us;
Yes, establish the work of our hands.

91.4:
He shall cover you with His feathers,
And under His wings you shall take refuge;
His truth shall be your shield and buckler.

91.7:
A thousand may fall at your side,
And ten thousand at your right hand;
But it shall not come near you.

91.15:
He shall call upon Me, and I will answer him;
I will be with him in trouble;
I will deliver him and honor him.

92.9:
For behold, Your enemies, O Lord,
For behold, Your enemies shall perish;
All the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.

92.11:
My eye also has seen my desire on my enemies;
My ears hear my desire on the wicked
Who rise up against me.

93.3:
The floods have lifted up, O Lord,
The floods have lifted up their voice;
The floods lift up their waves.

93.5:
Your testimonies are very sure;
Holiness adorns Your house,
O Lord, forever.

94.23:
He has brought on them their own iniquity,
And shall cut them off in their own wickedness;
The Lord our God shall cut them off.

96.10:
Say among the nations, “The Lord reigns;
The world also is firmly established,
It shall not be moved;
He shall judge the peoples righteously.”

97.1:
The Lord reigns;
Let the earth rejoice;
Let the multitude of isles be glad!

97.10:
You who love the Lord, hate evil!
He preserves the souls of His saints;
He delivers them out of the hand of the wicked.

98.1:
Oh, sing to the Lord a new song!
For He has done marvelous things;
His right hand and His holy arm have gained Him the victory.

99.1:
The Lord reigns;
Let the peoples tremble!
He dwells between the cherubim;
Let the earth be moved!

99.4:
The King’s strength also loves justice;
You have established equity;
You have executed justice and righteousness in Jacob.

99.6:
Moses and Aaron were among His priests,
And Samuel was among those who called upon His name;
They called upon the Lord, and He answered them.

99.8:
You answered them, O Lord our God;
You were to them God-Who-Forgives,
Though You took vengeance on their deeds.

99.9:
Exalt the Lord our God,
And worship at His holy hill;
For the Lord our God is holy.

100.3:
Know that the Lord, He is God;
It is He who has made us, and not we ourselves;
We are His people and the sheep of His pasture.

100.5:
For the Lord is good;
His mercy is everlasting,
And His truth endures to all generations.

101.3:
I will set nothing wicked before my eyes;
I hate the work of those who fall away;
It shall not cling to me.

102.2:
Do not hide Your face from me in the day of my trouble;
Incline Your ear to me;
In the day that I call, answer me speedily.

102.13:
You will arise and have mercy on Zion;
For the time to favor her,
Yes, the set time, has come.

102.24:
I said, “O my God,
Do not take me away in the midst of my days;
Your years are throughout all generations.

102.26:
They will perish, but You will endure;
Yes, they will all grow old like a garment;
Like a cloak You will change them,
And they will be changed.

104.8:
They went up over the mountains;
They went down into the valleys,
To the place which You founded for them.

104.26:
There the ships sail about;
There is that Leviathan
Which You have made to play there.

105.1:
Oh, give thanks to the Lord!
Call upon His name;
Make known His deeds among the peoples!

106.7:
Our fathers in Egypt did not understand Your wonders;
They did not remember the multitude of Your mercies,
But rebelled by the sea—the Red Sea.

106.9:
He rebuked the Red Sea also, and it dried up;
So He led them through the depths,
As through the wilderness.

106.43:
Many times He delivered them;
But they rebelled in their counsel,
And were brought low for their iniquity.

